# Persistence repositories — always use the base

## Standard CRUD (required)

Any Prisma adapter that implements `IRepository` **must** extend `PrismaCrudRepositoryBase`.

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class RolePrismaRepository extends PrismaCrudRepositoryBase<
  PrismaClient, 'authRole', Role, string, RoleFilter,
  RoleRow, AuthRoleWhereInput, AuthRoleWhereUniqueInput,
  ({} & AuthRoleCreateInput) | ({} & AuthRoleUncheckedCreateInput),
  ({} & AuthRoleUpdateInput) | ({} & AuthRoleUncheckedUpdateInput),
  AuthRoleOrderByWithRelationInput
> implements IRoleRepository {
  constructor(database: BasePrismaService<PrismaClient>) {
    super(database, 'authRole'); // generated client key only
  }
  // five mapping hooks — do not reimplement findPaged/create/update/delete
}
```

- Use generated delegate keys (`correspondenceNotification`, `authRole`, …). Stale names (`corr2Notification`) fail at runtime.
- `this.delegate` for the primary model; `this.client` / `$transaction` for other models or raw SQL.
- Preserve paging with `defaultPageSize()` instead of overriding `findPaged`.

## Exceptions (only these)

| Case | Use |
|------|-----|
| Custom port / multi-model / `$queryRaw` | `PrismaRepositoryBase` + typed `this.client` |
| Redis, cache, null, advisory lock | Existing non-Prisma adapter |

Never inject untyped `BasePrismaService` and never call missing delegates through a proxy.
